---

https://docs.oxide.computer/guides/operator/faq#_how_do_i_prepare_a_sled_for_removal_replacement

If Oxide Support have confirmed that a sled requires replacement, you can prepare the sled by reallocating workloads elsewhere using the Oxide CLI. You will need the serial number of the sled to be replaced <span style="font-family: 'Beleren', sans-serif; color: #00d892;">(Oxide Support can assist to confirm the serial number)</span>.

1. Using the Oxide CLI, obtain the UUID of the sled to replace:

```bash
oxide system hardware sled list | jq --arg sn "$SERIAL_NUMBER" '.[] | select(.baseboard.serial == $sn) | .id'
```

2. Set the sled as non-provisionable.

```bash
oxide system hardware sled set-provision-policy \
  --sled-id $SLED_UUID --state non_provisionable
```

3. Check for any instances present on the sled, and save the list into a file for reference:

```bash
oxide system hardware sled instance-list --sled-id $SLED_UUID |
  jq -r '.[].id' |
  tee /tmp/sled_xx_instances
```

4. Stop those instances, and wait for those instances to fully stop:

```bash
for instance_id in $(cat /tmp/sled_xx_instances); do
  oxide instance stop --instance $instance_id
done
```

5. Start the instances again (they will start on a different sled):

```bash
for instance_id in $(cat /tmp/sled_xx_instances); do
  oxide instance start --instance $instance_id
done
```

6. Confirm there are no longer any instances running on the sled to be replaced:

```bash
oxide system hardware sled instance-list --sled-id $SLED_UUID
```